  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA surface analysis shows a broad area of high pressure north of\nthe Great Lakes this morning while an inverted surface trough \nextends from the Ohio Valley to Northeast Ohio. Only a few light\nshowers are coming off the western basin of Lake Erie in a \nregion of favorable low level convergence that are shallow and mainly\nvisible on the DTW terminal radar. Otherwise, there is a lack \nof deep moisture overhead this morning but veering flow in the \nmoist low levels may support patchy drizzle, especially for \nareas from Akron to Youngstown. Later this afternoon the surface\ntrough retrogrades westward and moisture increases at 700mb \nacross NE Ohio. Several models suggest scattered light showers \nwill return across Northeast Ohio where lift continues along \nthe 850mb front. High temperatures will be similar to Monday in \nthe low to mid 60s. In addition northeast winds will be breezy \ndownwind of Lake Erie along the lakeshore and in Northwest Ohio\nwith gusts to around 30 mph. \n\nTonight will start off relatively quiet before the upper level \ntrough seen over Iowa this morning deepens across the Ohio Valley. \nScattered showers will expand after midnight as the trough \ncloses off across southern Indiana. Good coverage of showers are\nexpected initially along the I-77 corridor then drifting \nwestward through the day. There will also be a slight chance of \nthunderstorms with elevated instability as the cold pool aloft \nmoves overhead. Showers are expected to diminish quickly through\nthe evening. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nHigh pressure over Canada will expand south of the Great Lakes \non Thursday as the upper level trough deepens along the East \nCoast. Clouds will scatter out Thursday with lots of sun over \nthe weekend. The forecast is dry through next Monday with \ntemperatures gradually warming back towards normal. Overnight \nlows will be cool, generally in the low to mid 40s on Thursday \nnight and Friday night, then upper 40s(inland) to near\n50(lakeshore) for the weekend.",
